{
  "item": "DeathKnight01",
  "mu_name": "Death Knight",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain's MONSTER_MODEL_DEATH_KNIGHT = 29, so OpenMonsterModel loads Monster30.bmd; the server's type is MONSTER_DEATH_KNIGHT = 40. The client's name is 데쓰 나이트 (ZzzCharacter.cpp:13851-13859). OpenMU's Version075 LostTower.cs:855-885 names number 40 'Death Knight' at level 62 with 5500 health, 190-200 damage, 120 defense, MoveRange 3, AttackRange 1, ViewRange 7, AttackDelay 1800, no AttackSkill. 72 spots: 18 on Lost Tower 5, 13 on 6, 41 on 7.",
  "world": "losttower",
  "object_type": 40,
  "monster": {
    "model_index": 29,
    "scale": 1.3
  },
  "monster_from": "ZzzCharacter.cpp:13851-13859, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_DEATH_KNIGHT: the Giant Sword set and at once overwritten, `c->Weapon[0].Type = MODEL_LIGHTING_SWORD; c->Object.Scale = 1.3f;` (a shield and Level 1 commented out).",
  "right_hand": "Sword15",
  "right_hand_bone": "knife_gdf",
  "right_hand_from": "MODEL_LIGHTING_SWORD is Item/Sword15.bmd, cooked. Its bone is CreateCharacter's weapon switch: `case MODEL_DEATH_KNIGHT: c->Weapon[0].LinkBone = 30; c->Weapon[1].LinkBone = 39` (ZzzCharacter.cpp:12008-12011) -- 30 is knife_gdf, the player's grip name, under the right hand.",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "Seven actions, slots 0 to 6, exported with --actions=0,1,2,3,4,5,6. Keys: 12, 12, 7, 7, 7, 8, 11. 49 bones, a biped with the player's grip bones (knife_gdf 30, hand_bofdgne01 39). BoneHead is set for Type 3 and 29 in the Dark Knight's shared case (ZzzOpenData.cpp:3418-3420). OpenMonsterModel's default play speeds.",
  "sheets": {
    "as": "deathknight_as.png",
    "Polearms03": "deathknight_polearms03.png",
    "as_1": "deathknight_as_1.png",
    "shadow_b": "deathknight_shadow_b.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Four sheets, all .OZJ, no alpha: as (256 square) on the armour (1206 triangles), Polearms03 (64 square) on the halberd blades it wears on its back (104), as_1 (16 by 64) on mesh 3 (16), and shadow_b (16 square, the Shadow's ember) on one quad (2). Decoded under a deathknight_ prefix.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "as": "painted_steel",
    "Polearms03": "steel",
    "as_1": "painted_steel",
    "shadow_b": "painted_steel"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "Read off the sheets: as is bronze-brown plate in raised gold filigree with a skull at the lower right, lacquered armour as the Dark Knight's baron01, so painted_steel; Polearms03 is bright steel blades and a gilded haft, steel. as_1 is drawn as the glow below and its material is never seen.",
  "glow": {
    "as_1": {
      "scrolls_per_second": 1.0
    }
  },
  "glow_from": "MoveCharacterVisual's case MODEL_DEATH_KNIGHT: `o->BlendMesh = 3; o->BlendMeshTexCoordV = -(float)((int)(WorldTime) % 1000) * 0.001f;` (ZzzCharacter.cpp:6003-6006): mesh 3, the as_1 strip of orange fire, drawn additive and unlit with its V scrolled a whole sheet a second.",
  "effects_from": "The same case throws a BITMAP_FIRE particle at bone 2 (Bip01 Pelvis) one reference frame in two (:6007-6011). Not built yet: no monster fire particle is wired here.",
  "sounds_from": "ZzzOpenData.cpp:3409-3420, shared with the Dark Knight and the Titan: mDarkKnight1/2, mDarkKnightAttack1/2, mDarkKnightDie, SetMonsterSound(..., 15, 16, 17, 18, 19). Wired as deathknight_*, the Dark Knight's files.",
  "islands_from": "40 islands for 1328 triangles, all painted_steel: the islands carry no sheet, and the armour, the halberd blades and the glow strip are all metal, so the halberd's bright steel takes the armour's lacquer rather than its own. They arrived as skin, the monster profile's default.",
